!! Introduction:

<<twks-image "TiddlyCraftsCover.jpg" width:"250px" align:"right">>

TiddlyCrafts is my personal collection of TiddlyWiki plugins and tools. Some are small fixes I made for my own workflow; others started as experiments and ended up being useful. The collection grows slowly, usually when I run into a problem and can't find an existing plugin that solves it.

Most of them exist because I needed them myself. I'm sharing them here in case they're useful to someone else too. Since TiddlyWiki is what I use every day, I keep the plugins updated as I go.

Most of the plugins are small interface pieces: image figures, alert boxes, collapsible sections, and a few tools for notes and study. They don't try to change how TiddlyWiki works; they just add things I found myself missing. Use one or use all of them — whatever fits your setup.

You're welcome to use and change anything here. If a plugin is close to what you need but not quite right, open its source and edit it. That's how most of these started in the first place.

Feel free to explore, use, and adapt anything you find here. Installation is simple: just drag and drop a plugin into your TiddlyWiki.

''Made for my own workflow. Shared for yours.''

!! Installation:

There are three ways to install TiddlyCrafts plugins.

!!! 1. Plugin Library (Recommended)

; Step 1: Install the TiddlyCrafts Library

Drag the TiddlyCrafts Library link below into your TiddlyWiki and import it.

<div style="text-align: center;">
  <$link to="$:/config/TiddlyCraftsPluginLibrary" class="crft-lib">TiddlyCrafts Library</$link>
</div>

; Step 2: Manage your plugins

Open `$:/ControlPanel` ➡  `Plugins` ➡  `TiddlyCrafts Library` to install, update, or uninstall plugins.

<<twks-alerter type:"caution" text:"Do not install plugins marked ''Deprecated''.">>

!!! 2. Drag and Drop

Scroll down to the <kbd>Plugins</kbd> tab below and drag a plugin link from the list into your TiddlyWiki.

!!! 3. Node.js (local plugins)

If you use the Node.js edition of TiddlyWiki and prefer to use TiddlyCrafts plugins as local folders, clone the repository:

```
git clone git@github.com:uzvg/TiddlyCrafts.git
cd TiddlyCrafts
```

All TiddlyCrafts plugins are stored in the ''plugins'' folder. For the remaining steps, see [[Installing custom plugins on Node.js|https://tiddlywiki.com/#Installing%20custom%20plugins%20on%20Node.js]].

